# Managed by @plainconceptsplatform/workflows. Source: loops/templates/quality-gates/.semgrepignore. Update with `workflows update --force`; consumer edits may be overwritten.
# Generated agent workflow lock files are compiled output, never authored. The compiler emits
# quoted paths and secret-bearing env wiring that Semgrep's github-actions rules read as
# findings (gha-workflow-env-secret on the OTEL block, mutable-action-tag on pinned uses).
# The locks carry their own checks in agentics-checks.yml (version agreement, freshness,
# the needs lint); SAST scans the authored sources, not the compiler's output.
.github/workflows/*.lock.yml

# Third-party skill helper scripts that the agent harness installs under .agents/skills; they are
# vendored tooling for the coding agents, never part of the app, and a scan of them blocked a
# consumer's SAST job after this file replaced its own copy.
.agents/skills/*/scripts/
